{"agent":"impl-local-endpoint","data":{"budget":"local, offline, 15 min","claim":"kilo 7.8.18 (opencode fork, at [REDACTED:path]) accepts a provider with npm @ai-sdk/openai-compatible and options.baseURL, lists its model, keeps limit and tool_call, and resolves {env:NAME} for apiKey, but ONLY from the global config (HOME/.config/kilo/kilo.json); the same file in the project dir is refused with environment references are not allowed in project config. opencode itself is not installed: unverified. Tool-call reliability is NOT tested.","falsifier":"kilo config check reports a warning, or kilo models does not list the provider, on the rendered file; or a future kilo accepts env refs in project config (then the location stops mattering, not the claim).","item":"SW-local-endpoint","mechanism":"Setting HOME alone to the lane home redirects the global config dir, so a lane-private block needs no flag; keys stay env names; nothing enters the project.","probe":"kilo --version; kilo config check and kilo models in scratch HOME with a kilo.json in the project dir and in HOME/.config/kilo; kilo debug config; the rendered file from endpoint.write_private re-checked the same way","probe_output":"7.8.18; project dir: ConfigInvalidError 'environment references are not allowed in project config'; global dir: 'No config warnings.', models lists 'ddflow-lan-vllm/SERVED-MODEL-ID', debug config shows baseURL, limit {context,output}, tool_call true, apiKey substituted from env. No endpoint called, no key used.","question":"Does an installed opencode/kilo accept a custom OpenAI-compatible provider with a baseURL, and where may the lane-private block live?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e483890f5c8d5e45ac24cb8c1","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":115398,"schema":1,"subject":"R95eed7e146","ts":"2026-10-30T18:32:36.599161Z"}
